+      "Actions": "Multiattack. Make one Bite and one Stomp or Tail attack. The two attacks must have different targets.\nBite. Melee weapon attack, +11 to hit, 15-ft. reach, one target. On a hit, deal 39 (5d12 + 7) piercing damage. A Large or smaller creature hit must pass a DC 19 Dexterity save or be grappled (escape DC 19). The creature is restrained during the grapple, and Gishath cannot Bite another target until the grapple ends.\nSwallow. Make one Bite attack against a Large or smaller creature Gishath is grappling. On a hit, apply the Bite damage, swallow the creature, and end the grapple. A swallowed creature is blinded and restrained, has total cover from attacks and effects originating outside Gishath, and takes 21 (6d6) acid damage at the start of each of Gishath’s turns.\nIf an individual swallowed creature deals at least 30 damage to Gishath in one turn, Gishath must make a DC 18 Constitution save at that turn’s end. On a failure, it ejects every swallowed creature. Each lands prone in a space within 10 ft. of it. If Gishath dies, a swallowed creature is no longer restrained by it and can spend 20 ft. of movement to exit the body prone.\nStomp. Melee weapon attack, +11 to hit, 10-ft. reach, one target. On a hit, deal 29 (5d8 + 7) bludgeoning damage. The target must pass a DC 19 Strength save or fall prone.\nTail. Melee weapon attack, +11 to hit, 15-ft. reach, one target. On a hit, deal 25 (4d8 + 7) bludgeoning damage.",
